[Event "Queen's Gambit"]
[StudyName "Queen's Gambit"]
[ChapterName "Queen's Gambit Declined: Orthodox, Tartakower"]
[Orientation "white"]

1. d4 d5 2. c4 {The Queen's Gambit. It is not really a gambit: if Black takes, you win the pawn back.} e6 {Black declines and keeps a solid centre.} 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. Bg5 {Pins the knight that defends d5. [%cal Gg5f6,Rf6d5] [%csl Yd5]} Be7 5. e3 O-O 6. Nf3 h6 7. Bh4 b6 {The Tartakower: Black prepares ...Bb7 and ...Ne4 ideas.} 8. cxd5 Nxd5 9. Bxe7 Qxe7 10. Nxd5 exd5 11. Rc1 Be6 12. Qa4 c5 13. Qa3 Rc8 14. Bb5 a6 15. dxc5 bxc5 16. O-O Ra7 17. Be2 Nd7 18. Nd4 Qf8 {A famous, perfectly balanced position.}

[Event "Queen's Gambit"]
[StudyName "Queen's Gambit"]
[ChapterName "Queen's Gambit Declined: Exchange"]
[Orientation "white"]

1. d4 d5 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. cxd5 {The Exchange Variation: a clear plan, the minority attack with b4-b5.} exd5 5. Bg5 Be7 6. e3 O-O 7. Bd3 Nbd7 8. Qc2 Re8 9. Nge2 Nf8 10. O-O c6 11. Rab1 {Ready for b4-b5 to damage Black's queenside pawns.}

[Event "Queen's Gambit"]
[StudyName "Queen's Gambit"]
[ChapterName "Queen's Gambit Accepted"]
[Orientation "white"]

1. d4 d5 2. c4 dxc4 {Black takes the pawn, but cannot keep it for long.} 3. Nf3 Nf6 4. e3 e6 5. Bxc4 c5 6. O-O a6 7. Qe2 b5 8. Bb3 Bb7 9. Rd1 Nbd7 {White has a lead in development and the centre to play for.}
